## What changed

- Skill names: ce-retro is retro, ce-compound is compound.
- Config and scratch paths: .compound-engineering is .brigade.
- Calls to upstream-only skills (ce-setup, ce-plan, ce-noslop, ce-simplify-code, superpowers:test-driven-development) point to the project's own standards file, planning flow and skills.
- CONCEPTS.md and CODING_STANDARDS.md map to the files a project names in .brigade/config.yaml.

The two commits that vendor and adjust these skills are separate in git history, so `git diff` between them shows every change.
